<Base title="Postdoc and PhD positions in nanophotonics" description="Open positions in experimental nanophotonics and quantum optics at the Niels Bohr Institute, University of Copenhagen: postdoctoral positions, a fixed-term assistant professorship, and PhD and master's projects. Salaries, benefits and how to apply.">
<section>
  <div class="wrap two top">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Join us in Copenhagen</p>
      <h1>Founding members wanted</h1>
      <p>We are building a new research group and looking for curious experimentalists who want to explore fundamental questions at the boundaries of optics, materials, and quantum science. The people who join now will be founding members of the lab — building the first experiments with us, setting up instruments as they are delivered, and producing its earliest results.</p>
      <div class="pos"><b>Postdoctoral positions</b><span>Experimental nanophotonics and quantum optics · <a href="https://employment.ku.dk/all-vacancies?show=167960">Posting and application</a></span></div>
      <div class="pos"><b>Assistant Professor (fixed term)</b><span>Nanophotonics of quantum and 2D materials · posting coming soon; informal inquiries welcome now</span></div>
      <div class="pos"><b>PhD and master's projects</b><span>Write to us</span></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:22px;margin-top:28px">Working in Denmark</h2>
      <p>Copenhagen is a good place to do this work and to live. Postdoc salaries follow the Danish collective agreement for academics, with a 17% employer pension contribution on top and a negotiable supplement; international researchers can qualify for a reduced flat tax rate. The University's <a href="https://ism.ku.dk/">International Staff Mobility</a> office supports arriving staff with residence permits, housing, and family matters, and no Danish is required.</p>
      <p>Informal inquiries are welcome — send a CV and a short note on your interests to <a href="mailto:maiken.mikkelsen@nbi.ku.dk">maiken.mikkelsen@nbi.ku.dk</a>.</p>
    </div>
